{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 23, "model_name": "qwen/qwen3.5-397b-a17b", "content": "**Chasing Cherry Blossoms in Kyoto**\n\nStepping off the Shinkansen in Kyoto felt like entering a different era. The air was crisp, carrying the faint, sweet scent of sakura. My first stop was the Arashiyama Bamboo Grove. Walking beneath those towering green stalks, with sunlight filtering through in dappled patterns, was strangely meditative. The sound of the wind rustling the leaves is something I'll never forget.\n\nLater, I wandered through the historic Gion district. Traditional wooden machiya houses lined the narrow streets, and I caught a fleeting glimpse of a geisha hurrying to an appointment. It was a magical moment that felt straight out of a movie. Of course, no trip to Japan is complete without the food. I indulged in steaming bowls of ramen at a tiny shop where the chef had been perfecting his broth for decades. The rich, savory flavor was life-changing.\n\nThe highlight, however, was visiting Fushimi Inari Taisha at sunset. Climbing through thousands of vibrant orange torii gates as the sky turned pink and gold was breathtaking. The silence up the mountain, broken only by the occasional temple bell, offered a profound sense of peace.\n\nJapan blends the ancient and the futuristic seamlessly. One minute you are surrounded by neon lights in Tokyo, and the next, you are bowing respectfully at a centuries-old shrine. This trip wasn't just a vacation; it was a lesson in mindfulness, beauty, and hospitality. I left with a full stomach, a full heart, and a promise to return soon. If you haven't visited yet, put it at the top of your bucket list. You won't regret it.", "logprobs": [{"token": "**", "logprob": -0.046162672}, {"token": "Ch", "logprob": -0.03992872}, {"token": "asing", "logprob": -2.5788903}, {"token": " Cherry", "logprob": -4.3154694e-05}, {"token": " Bloss", "logprob": -1.7881409e-06}, {"token": "oms", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " in"